Both bugs fixed. Results now match expectations: **Done: 10, Failed: 2, Stuck: 0**.

Summary of the two fixes:

1. **`job_queue.py:19-22`** — Moved `job["status"] = "processing"` *before* the `await asyncio.sleep(0.01)`. The `await` yielded to the event loop while the job was still "pending", allowing all workers to dequeue the same job. In cooperative async, synchronous code between await points is atomic, so claiming the job before yielding eliminates the TOCTOU race.

2. **`worker.py:19`** — Added `queue.fail(job["id"], str(e))`. The except block was swallowing exceptions without telling the queue, so failed jobs stayed in `"processing"` forever — never retried and never marked `"failed"`.
